SUBJECT (player vocation BR; canon identity): BR Brinecaller, the elemental control caster of salt and tide: the magic of an inland sea that died within a generation. The stranger whose hand the Loosed held: Hasmik of the Brine, a salt-witch of the inland sea. Weapons: staff (driftwood lashed with rope and shells) and wand. Class item: the brine-flask, a glass flask of sea water from before the Great Ebb, carried in the LEFT hand where the kit allows. Armour class: light. The hero's salt is NOT Kathara's salt: it is grey-green, gritty, jagged, mixed with sand and weed, crystals growing at crooked angles, never a perfect shape. The water is turbid teal with foam and weed, never clear blue. The only 'pattern' of the vocation is the tide-line: dried concentric salt rings on cloth, uneven, like a retreating tide. Nothing is symmetric, not even the crystals; the salt is always lopsided to the RIGHT side.
DIRECTION DESIGN (base design; the SIGNATURE PUSH and PALETTE V2 below override any size or colour in it): DIRECTION A - DEAD-SEA WITCH (the tide witch; long staff and net). SILHOUETTE: a tall staff line; many wrapped layers of kelp-brown cloth with a heavy, curved hem. A fishing-net shawl in sea-grey linen across the shoulders, with a few cork floats and shells. Grey-green SALT grows as angular clusters on the RIGHT shoulder and runs down the RIGHT sleeve; the left side is clean. The headscarf is a SHORT KNOTTED WRAP with NO long tail; a thin murky-teal trim on its edge. A thin teal sash. PROPS: a crooked driftwood staff in the RIGHT hand, 1.25H (500 px) tall, lashed with rope in two places, three or four shells and a glass float hanging near the head. A bandolier of THREE small brine-flasks across the chest (cork-stoppered glass wrapped in cord net, 0.10H (40 px) each); one flask carries salt crust growing from its mouth downward (physical, not glowing). OSRIC'S LANTERN (carried by every hero from A1-Q2): a small plain old iron watch-lantern, 0.12H (48 px) tall, ONE simple hinged hood flap, NO slats and NO notches (it must never look like the Exhumer's five-slat class lantern), unlit; hanging on a short chain behind the RIGHT hip (seen in the RIGHT and BACK views). This is the exception to the left-hand class-item convention: while the staff is held the flasks are worn on the body. HANDS: LEFT hand = the held hand: a shell bracelet and one big tide-line stain on the sleeve cuff. RIGHT hand: bare on the staff, one small tarnished silver ring on the ring finger. HEM: two or three big, distorted tide-line rings. ASYMMETRY: the LEFT view shows the clean left side, the shell bracelet and the flask bandolier; the RIGHT view shows the salt-crusted shoulder and sleeve, the staff hand and Osric's Lantern; the BACK view shows the net shawl, the knotted scarf and the lantern.
SIGNATURE PUSH (exaggerate these class features; they override the base sizes): Exaggerate the Brinecaller's signature: a LARGE cluster of angular, irregular pale grey-green salt crystals grows over the RIGHT shoulder like a pauldron and runs down the right sleeve; the crooked driftwood staff (about 1.35H) in the right hand is crowned with a big salt-crystal cluster, rope bindings, shells and a hanging green glass float; a bandolier of three bigger brine flasks across the chest with churning murky-teal water and salt crusting from the necks; a fishing-net shawl with glass floats and shells; flowing teal robes with a curling wave-shaped hem marked by two or three tide lines; a short knotted headscarf with no tail; shell bracelet on the left wrist.
PALETTE V2 (overrides every colour above; rich but not neon): Signature: DEEP SEA TEAL + TURQUOISE + SEAFOAM. Robes and smock deep sea teal #11606A shading to turquoise #2FA3A0 with seafoam highlights #CFEDE6; salt crystals pale grey-green #CFDCC8 (never pure white, always irregular and gritty); kelp green #3E5A36; rope sand gold #C9A55C; shells cream #EFE3C8; a few small coral-red accent beads #D9574A; sea water murky teal with foam, never clear blue.
DIFFERENTIATION: Variant B is a short, low, wading figure in a quilted kelp smock with rolled trousers, wading wraps with salt crust on one leg, a close knitted cap, one big round flask in a rope net in the left hand, a short whale-bone wand and a small stoneware salt-crock; A is the long lopsided silhouette with a tall staff, a net shawl, a flask bandolier and a short knotted headscarf. The other variant is designed independently with a different silhouette, shape structure, cloth/armour construction and accessory placement; do not reuse any of it, and keep the same canonical identity, size and signature prop or behaviour. Against the lookalikes the concept doc lists for this vocation: NOT the Lye Priest (F13, white porcelain mask, black-and-white robes), NOT the Salt-Clan (D06, bone-white glaze), NOT the Salt Pillar (P12, pure white salt #EDEAE0), NOT Kathara (clear teal, perfect symmetric crystals), NOT the Salted Dead or the Brine-Embalmer (U13, U14: stiff pale cloth wrapped in a white salt shell). Hero salt is grey-green, gritty and lopsided; water is turbid; no mask; nothing symmetric. Avoid: no clear ice-blue, no glowing orb, no symmetric crystals, no white porcelain mask, no black-and-white robe, no pure white salt, no clear blue water, no oilskin coat (Maelys), no wide-brim hat (Exhumer), no long trailing cloth tail from the head.
